Description: Wild OS controls in Kvantum
 Four changes so the WildOS Kvantum theme can draw the design's controls.
 .
 Default buttons: a theme can draw the default (primary) button per state
 ("button-default-normal", "-focused", "-pressed", "-toggled") as a solid
 accent button; its label then uses the highlighted-text colour. Without
 those elements Kvantum keeps its stock overlay.
 .
 Menus: a new [General] menu_padding sets the space between a menu's edge
 and its items, so a menu can have a 14 px rounded corner and 6 px of
 padding. The blur radius cap for menus and tooltips rises from 10 to 16 to
 match such corners.
 .
 Focus rectangles may use up to 6 px of the theme's focus frame, so the
 ring keeps rounded corners.
 .
 Accent: a theme can list the colours it draws its accent with
 ([General] accent_colors); they are swapped for the accent picked in the
 system settings (kdeglobals [General] AccentColor) when the SVG loads.
Author: Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>
Forwarded: not-needed

